{"benchmark": "ifeval", "task_id": "1021", "sample_idx": 42, "model_name": "meta/llama-3.3-70b-instruct", "content": "PARAGRAPH 1\nTHE GIVEN SENTENCE \"IF THE LAW IS BAD, YOU SHOULD NOT FOLLOW IT\" IS A STATEMENT THAT RAISES SEVERAL QUESTIONS ABOUT THE NATURE OF AUTHORITY AND MORALITY. ON ONE HAND, IT CAN BE ARGUED THAT THIS SENTENCE ENCOURAGES CRITICAL THINKING AND EVALUATION OF THE LAWS THAT GOVERN SOCIETY. BY SUGGESTING THAT NOT ALL LAWS ARE CREATED EQUAL, IT IMPLIES THAT INDIVIDUALS HAVE A RESPONSIBILITY TO ASSESS THE MERITS OF EACH LAW AND DECIDE WHETHER IT IS JUST OR NOT. HOWEVER, THIS APPROACH CAN ALSO BE SEEN AS PROBLEMATIC, AS IT MAY LEAD TO A BREAKDOWN IN SOCIAL ORDER AND RESPECT FOR AUTHORITY.\n\nPARAGRAPH 2\nFURTHERMORE, THE SENTENCE \"IF THE LAW IS BAD, YOU SHOULD NOT FOLLOW IT\" OVERSIMPLIFIES THE COMPLEXITIES OF LEGAL AND MORAL FRAMEWORKS. IN REALITY, LAWS ARE OFTEN THE RESULT OF COMPLEX NEGOTIATIONS AND COMPROMISES BETWEEN DIFFERENT INTEREST GROUPS AND STAKEHOLDERS. TO SIMPLY DISMISS A LAW AS \"BAD\" AND REFUSE TO FOLLOW IT OVERLOOKS THE POSSIBILITY THAT THE LAW MAY SERVE A GREATER GOOD, EVEN IF IT IS IMPERFECT. ADDITIONALLY, THIS SENTENCE DOES NOT PROVIDE ANY CLEAR GUIDANCE ON HOW TO DETERMINE WHETHER A LAW IS \"BAD\" OR NOT, LEAVING INDIVIDUALS TO RELY ON THEIR OWN SUBJECTIVE JUDGMENT AND POTENTIALLY LEADING TO CONFUSION AND CONFLICT.", "logprobs": [{"token": "PAR", "logprob": -1.0728830375228426e-06}, {"token": "AGR", "logprob": -2.455681169521995e-05}, {"token": "APH", "logprob": -1.0728830375228426e-06}, {"token": " ", "logprob": 0.0}, {"token": "1", "logprob": 0.0}, {"token": "\n", "logprob": -8.22540732769994e-06}, {"token": "THE", "logprob": -0.0010343207977712154}, {"token": " GIVEN", "logprob": -1.2245818376541138}, {"token": " SENT", "logprob": -4.2437604861333966e-05}, {"token": "ENCE", "logprob": 0.0}, {"token": " \"", "logprob": -0.026191525161266327}, {"token": "IF", "logprob": -1.597391747054644e-05}, {"token": " THE", "logprob": 0.0}